# R23 the Silent Church as a shelter. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ arrive
Narrator: The vigil's song stops at the door as if cut with a knife. Pews have been dragged into rows for the sick, the children are asleep on the altar steps in a heap of coats, and a knight in marble twice a man's height stands in the nave, listening for the fire.
set wv_shelter_seen
-> END

~ marble
Narrator: The knight's voice arrives in your mind without passing through your ears.
man_in_marble [neutral]: Bring them under my roof and I will keep the song from them. I cannot leave. I can stand, and I can listen. That is all I have ever been good for.
-> marble_menu

~ marble_menu
* [if flag.sleep_count >= 1] Tell him who is sheltered -> marble_count
* Ask what the song does -> marble_song
* Ask if the church will hold -> marble_hold
* Leave him to his watch -> END

~ marble_count
man_in_marble [neutral]: I have counted them. Those who are inside I will keep. Those who are outside, I cannot.
-> marble_menu

~ marble_song
man_in_marble [sad]: It finds the weak place in the mind and makes it sing. Under this roof the weak place is just a place.
-> marble_menu

~ marble_hold
man_in_marble [neutral]: It will hold against the song. Against the fire it is only wood and stone. Keep the fire away from it.
-> marble_menu

~ weston
weston_murdoch [smile]: The Brightsingers' hymns cannot carry here either. I sing them anyway, softly, so the children have something. Go and win. If you cannot win, then go and be seen trying.
-> END
